ADDGROUP(8)                 System Manager's Manual                ADDGROUP(8)

NAME
       addgroup - add a group to the system

SYNOPSIS
       addgroup [options] GROUP
       addgroup --system [options] GROUP
       adduser USER GROUP

DESCRIPTION
       addgroup adds groups to the system.  It is the same program as
       adduser(8), invoked under the name addgroup so that group creation is
       the default action.

       addgroup GROUP
              Create a group.  A group id is allocated from FIRST_GID..LAST_GID
              (1000..59999) unless --gid is given.

       addgroup --system GROUP
              Create a group from the system range (100..999).

       adduser USER GROUP
              Add an existing user to an existing group.

OPTIONS
       --system              create a system group
       --gid ID              force the group id
       --firstgid ID, --lastgid ID
                             override the group id range
       --allow-all-names, --allow-bad-names
                             relax the group name check
       --quiet, --verbose, --debug
                             adjust the amount of output
       --conf FILE           configuration file (accepted, unused)
       --help                display this help
       --version             display version

FILES
       /etc/group    group database

NOTES
       Only the superuser may add groups.

SEE ALSO
       adduser(8), passwd(1), groups(1)

